  "title": "Markdown is not agent memory",
  "summary": "Some of the most capable agents in production keep their memory in plain markdown files, and for a single agent and a single user it is hard to beat. The pattern breaks in predictable places: at scale, as facts change and errors compound, and under concurrent agents.",
